title: '[pallet-revive] align terminate precompile with opcodes'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    This PR aligns the terminate precompile with the opcodes.

    - The precompile now pays out the balance immediately and only deletes the contract if this transaction created it, as `SELFDESTRUCT` does.
    - The deposit is no longer refunded when terminate is called.
    - TerminateArgs and schedule_termination are gone; the scheduling map just stores the beneficiary.

    Tests:
    - Tests that relied on deleting a contract from an earlier transaction now create and terminate it in the same call.
    - Tests that call terminate on an older contract now assert the contract survives.
    - Removed tests whose scenario can no longer happen (deposit refund at call time and several payers' deposits being refunded at termination).
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-types
  bump: patch
